<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valerian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">captured <a href="/years/260">260 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Emperor Valerian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Valerian was a Roman emperor of the mid-third century CE who campaigned against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>. In 260 CE he was captured by the Sasanian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shapur-i">Shapur I</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-edessa">Battle of Edessa</a>, becoming the first Roman emperor taken prisoner by a foreign enemy. He died in captivity, and accounts of the Sasanian Empire treat his capture as a symbol of the dynasty's early military triumph.</p></div>
